{"key":"apphy2-mcq-021","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"twice as large","working":"The ideal gas law can be written as PV = N k_B T, which gives P = (N k_B T) / V. If temperature T and volume V are kept constant, the pressure P is directly proportional to the number of molecules N. Therefore, doubling N results in doubling P, making the pressure twice as large.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":347,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":347,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":263,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":106,"reasoningTokens":157},"totalTokens":610,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":157,"promptTokenCount":347,"candidatesTokenCount":106,"totalTokenCount":610,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":347}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":106}]},"reasoningTokens":157,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3455,"keyed_label":"C"}
