{"key":"apphy2-mcq-022","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"twice as large","working":"The rate of heat transfer by conduction through a rod is given by Fourier's law: Q/t = k * A * ΔT / L, where k is thermal conductivity, A is cross-sectional area, ΔT is the temperature difference across the ends, and L is the length of the rod. Both rods have equal dimensions (same A and L) and the same temperature difference (ΔT). Therefore, the conduction rate is directly proportional to the thermal conductivity k. Since Rod A has twice the thermal conductivity of Rod B (k_A = 2 * k_B), the conduction rate through Rod A is twice as large as through Rod B.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":359,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":359,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":364,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":172,"reasoningTokens":192},"totalTokens":723,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":192,"promptTokenCount":359,"candidatesTokenCount":172,"totalTokenCount":723,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":359}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":172}]},"reasoningTokens":192,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3086,"keyed_label":"C"}
